# D09 services/daemons and D10 software
@phase 800
[D09-001] CMD server 60
cmd: srv systemctl list-units --all --no-pager --no-legend --full 2>&1
out: systemctl-units.txt
req: is_systemd
purpose: All loaded units with load/active/sub state.
expect: UNIT LOAD ACTIVE SUB DESCRIPTION lines.
empty: Not applicable without systemd.
value: Running/failed services, units loaded from unusual paths.
ref: draft-4a

[D09-002] CMD server 60
cmd: srv systemctl list-unit-files --no-pager --no-legend 2>&1
out: systemctl-unit-files.txt
req: is_systemd
purpose: Every unit file with enabled/disabled/static/masked state.
expect: UNIT FILE STATE VENDOR PRESET.
empty: Not applicable without systemd.
value: Enabled units that are not vendor-preset; masked security services.
ref: draft-4a

[D09-003] FUNC server 600
cmd: systemd_service_details
out: services-detail
req: is_systemd
purpose: For every service: systemctl show (ExecStart, FragmentPath, DropInPaths, MainPID, timestamps, User) and systemctl cat.
expect: services-detail/<unit>.show.txt and .cat.txt.
empty: Not applicable without systemd.
value: Exact command each service runs, since when, from which file and drop-ins.
ref: draft-4a

[D09-004] DERIVED mixed 900
cmd: services_table
out: services.csv
purpose: Build services.csv: one row per service/daemon with state, start time, main PID, binary, binary SHA-256, user, unit file times (when installed/enabled), owning package, origin.
expect: CSV with header; one row per service (systemd or init scripts).
empty: Never empty on a normal host.
value: Answers 'which daemons run, since when, installed when and from which package or by hand'.
ref: draft-4a

[D09-005] FUNC kit 120
cmd: listeners_without_service
out: listeners-without-service.txt
purpose: Listening sockets whose process is not part of any service unit / init script.
expect: Usually only the examiner's tools or nothing.
empty: Empty is normal.
value: Backdoor listeners started by hand or by an exploit.
ref: draft-4a

[D09-006] CMD server 60
cmd: srv service --status-all 2>&1; srv chkconfig --list 2>&1; srv rc-status -a 2>&1; srv rc-update show -v 2>&1; srv initctl list 2>&1; srv sv status /var/service/* 2>&1
out: non-systemd-services.txt
req: ! is_systemd || has service || has chkconfig || has rc-status
purpose: Service state from SysV/OpenRC/Upstart/runit tools.
expect: Service status lines from whichever tool exists.
empty: Sections for missing tools report 'command not found'.
value: Same as systemd units for non-systemd systems.
ref: draft-1

[D09-007] CMD server 60
cmd: srv systemctl --failed --all --no-pager 2>&1; echo; srv systemctl get-default 2>&1; srv runlevel 2>&1
out: failed-units-target.txt
req: is_systemd
purpose: Failed units and default target/runlevel.
expect: 0 loaded units listed (normal) or failed units; graphical/multi-user target.
empty: Not applicable without systemd.
value: Security services that crashed or were stopped.
ref: UAC:runlevel

@phase 900
[D10-001] FUNC mixed 900
cmd: packages_list
out: packages
purpose: Installed packages with version, architecture, install time, vendor/packager and signature (dpkg, rpm, apk, pacman, zypper, xbps, portage, nix, ...).
expect: packages/<manager>-installed.tsv per package manager present.
empty: Not applicable for systems without a package manager.
value: Inventory of software and when each package was installed.
ref: draft-4b

[D10-002] DERIVED mixed 900
cmd: software_table
out: software.csv
purpose: Build software.csv: name, version, arch, install time, last change, how installed (repo/local file/manual), source repo, who installed (when logged).
expect: CSV, one row per package plus snap/flatpak/pip/npm/gem entries.
empty: Never empty on a normal host.
value: One table for 'what is installed, when and from where'.
ref: draft-4b

[D10-003] COPY kit 1800
cmd: -R /var/log/dpkg.log* /var/log/apt /var/log/yum.log* /var/log/dnf.log* /var/log/dnf.rpm.log* /var/log/dnf.librepo.log* /var/log/hawkey.log* /var/log/zypp /var/log/zypper.log* /var/log/pacman.log* /var/log/installer /var/log/anaconda /root/anaconda-ks.cfg /root/original-ks.cfg /var/log/apk.log /var/log/xbps* /var/log/emerge.log /var/log/portage
purpose: Package manager logs (install/upgrade/remove history), installer logs.
expect: Rotated logs including .gz.
empty: Only the package manager in use leaves logs (Alpine keeps none).
value: When and what was installed or REMOVED; yum.log on EL5-7 has no year (inferred from file names/times).
ref: draft-13.5; draft-yum

[D10-004] COPY kit 1800
cmd: -R /var/lib/dpkg/status /var/lib/dpkg/status-old /var/lib/dpkg/diversions /var/lib/dpkg/statoverride /var/lib/dpkg/info /var/lib/apt/extended_states /var/lib/rpm /usr/lib/sysimage/rpm /var/lib/yum/history /var/lib/yum/yumdb /var/lib/dnf /usr/lib/sysimage/libdnf5 /usr/lib/sysimage/dnf /lib/apk/db /etc/apk /var/lib/pacman/local /var/lib/zypp /var/db/xbps /var/db/pkg /var/lib/snapd/state.json /var/lib/flatpak/repo/config /var/lib/flatpak/app
purpose: Raw package databases (dpkg, rpm, yum/dnf/dnf5 history, apk, pacman, zypp, xbps, portage, snapd, flatpak).
expect: Database files; dnf5 history location varies between distros, so all candidates are copied.
empty: Only databases of the managers in use.
value: Re-analysis offline without trusting the server's package tools; history databases hold every transaction with user and command line.
ref: draft-23.4 no.3; draft-yum

[D10-005] FUNC mixed 600
cmd: pkg_history
out: package-history
purpose: Transaction history: yum/dnf history database read with sqlite3 (copy, read-only) plus the server's yum/dnf history (cache-only), apt history, zypp history, pacman log, snap changes.
expect: Transactions with id, time, user, command line, actions (Install/Erase/Update...).
empty: EMPTY when no history exists.
value: Who installed or removed what and when; differences between DB and tool output indicate tampering.
ref: draft-13.5; draft-yum

[D10-006] COPY kit 600
cmd: -R /etc/apt/sources.list /etc/apt/sources.list.d /etc/apt/trusted.gpg /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d /etc/apt/preferences /etc/apt/preferences.d /etc/apt/auth.conf /etc/apt/auth.conf.d /usr/share/keyrings /etc/yum.conf /etc/yum.repos.d /etc/yum/vars /etc/dnf/dnf.conf /etc/dnf/vars /etc/dnf/protected.d /etc/pki/rpm-gpg /etc/zypp /etc/pacman.conf /etc/pacman.d /etc/apk/repositories /etc/apk/keys /etc/xbps.d /etc/portage/repos.conf
purpose: Repository definitions and trusted signing keys of every package manager.
expect: Repo files and GPG keys.
empty: Only for managers in use.
value: Foreign repositories and keys, gpgcheck=0, credentials in auth.conf.
sensitive: yes
ref: draft-yum; draft-4b

[D10-007] CMD server 60
cmd: srv rpm -q gpg-pubkey --qf '%{NAME}-%{VERSION}-%{RELEASE}\t%{INSTALLTIME:date}\t%{SUMMARY}\n' 2>&1
out: rpm-imported-keys.txt
req: has rpm
purpose: GPG keys imported into the rpm database, with import time.
expect: One line per key with packager identity.
empty: Not applicable on non-rpm systems.
value: A key imported recently by an attacker allows malicious packages to install silently.
ref: draft-yum

[D10-008] FUNC mixed 300
cmd: lang_packages
out: language-packages
purpose: Software outside the system package manager: pip (each interpreter, dist-info INSTALLER/direct_url.json), npm global, gem, cargo, go bin, composer, snap, flatpak, AppImage, conda.
expect: One list per ecosystem.
empty: EMPTY when none is installed.
value: Attackers install tools with pip/npm/go; direct_url.json shows installation from a URL or file.
ref: draft-4b

[D10-009] FUNC kit 1800
cmd: unpackaged_executables
out: unpackaged-executables.tsv
purpose: Executables in system and common folders that no package owns (dpkg/rpm/apk/pacman file lists), with hash, owner, times and ELF type.
expect: TSV of unowned executables; local admin tools appear here too.
empty: Empty on clean package-only hosts.
value: Manually dropped binaries (backdoors, tools) stand out.
ref: draft-4b

[D10-010] COPY kit 3600
cmd: -R /var/cache/apt/archives /var/cache/yum /var/cache/dnf /var/cache/zypp/packages /var/cache/pacman/pkg /var/cache/apk /etc/apk/cache /root/.cache/pip
purpose: Package caches (downloaded packages, including ones already removed).
expect: *.deb/*.rpm/*.apk/*.pkg.tar.* files.
empty: Caches are often cleaned.
value: Proof of a package that was installed and later removed; original files of tampered packages.
ref: draft-14.12

@phase 2450
[D10-020] FUNC mixed 7200
cmd: package_integrity
out: package-integrity
purpose: Verify installed files against the package database (dpkg md5sums computed by C0F, rpm -Va, pacman -Qkk, apk audit).
expect: List of changed files with the type of change (size, mode, hash, owner).
empty: Empty means no difference (config files usually differ and are marked).
value: Replaced system binaries (ls, ps, sshd, login) are the classic userland rootkit.
ref: draft-16; UAC:packages_integrity
